esktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-2-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/assets/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/neo4j_workflow3_cross_policy_lineage.json)\n  - [neo4j_summary_statistics.json](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-2-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/assets/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/neo4j_summary_statistics.json)\n  - [neo4j_schema_constraints_and_indexes.json](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-2-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/assets/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/neo4j_schema_constraints_and_indexes.json)\n\n### 3.2. Hugging Face Open-Weight Model Services \u0026 Inference Router API\n- **Role:** LLM synthesis engine for grounded answer generation without Cypher hallucination (Section 4.2 Stage 4).\n- **Endpoints Probed:**\n  1. *Model Metadata API:* `GET https://huggingface.co/api/models/Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct` (HTTP 200 OK).\n  2. *Inference Router Catalog:* `GET https://router.huggingface.co/v1/models` (HTTP 200 OK, 118 models available).\n  3. *Chat Completions Endpoint:* `POST https://router.huggingface.co/v1/chat/completions` (HTTP 401 Unauthorized without bearer token).\n- **Observed Schema \u0026 Contract Details:**\n  - Catalog Schema: `$.data[*].{id: string, object: 'model', created: int, owned_by: string}`.\n  - Model Attributes: Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct has 7.6B parameters (BF16), inference status `\"warm\"`, native Jinja chat template with `\u003c|im_start|\u003e` and `\u003c|im_end|\u003e` delimiters.\n  - Telemetry Error Handling: Unauthenticated requests return HTTP 401 with `x-request-id` and CloudFront headers. Authentication requires header `Authorization: Bearer \u003cHF_TOKEN\u003e` with `inference.serverless.write` permission.\n- **Saved Ground-Truth Payloads:**\n  - [hf_model_api_qwen25_7b.json](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-2-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/assets/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/hf_model_api_qwen25_7b.json)\n  - [hf_router_v1_models.json](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-2-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/assets/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/hf_router_v1_models.json)\n  - [hf_router_v1_models_headers.txt](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-2-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/assets/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/hf_router_v1_models_headers.txt)\n  - [hf_chat_completions_unauth_error.json](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-2-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/assets/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/hf_chat_completions_unauth_error.json)\n  - [hf_chat_completions_401_headers.txt](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-2-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/assets/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/hf_chat_completions_401_headers.txt)\n\n### 3.3. Federal Register API v1\n- **Role:** Source of authoritative regulatory publication metadata and CFR references cited in node detail drawer and LLM provenance blocks (Section 3.1 Item 5, Section 4.2 Stage 5).\n- **Endpoint:** `GET https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/documents/2023-24455.json` (HTTP 200 OK, Content-Length: 100,483 bytes).\n- **Authentication:** None required.\n- **Observed Schema:** `$.document_number` (`\"2023-24455\"`), `$.citation` (`\"88 FR 77676\"`), `$.effective_on` (`\"2024-01-01\"`), `$.title`, `$.abstract`, `$.body_html_url`, `$.pdf_url`, and `$.cfr_references[*].{title: int, part: string}` linking 42 CFR Parts 409, 410, 414, 424, 484, 488, 489.\n- **Saved Ground-Truth Payload:**\n  - [federal_register_rule_2023_24455.json](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-2-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/assets/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/federal_register_rule_2023_24455.json)\n\n### 3.4. Electronic Code of Federal Regulations (eCFR) API\n- **Role:** Authoritative legal text verification for CFR citations (42 CFR § 410.36, 42 CFR § 414.1650) cited in node detail drawer (Section 3.1 Item 5).\n- **Endpoints:**\n  1. `GET https://www.ecfr.gov/api/versioner/v1/titles.json` (HTTP 200 OK).\n  2. `GET https://www.ecfr.gov/api/search/v1/results?query=lymphedema` (HTTP 200 OK, 57 results).\n- **Observed Schema:** `$.results[*].hierarchy.{title: '42', chapter: 'IV', subchapter: 'B', part: '414', subpart: 'Q', section: '414.1650'}`. Headings detail `Payment for Lymphedema Compression Treatment Items`.\n- **Saved Ground-Truth Payloads:**\n  - [ecfr_titles.json](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-2-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/assets/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/ecfr_titles.json)\n  - [ecfr_search_lymphedema.json](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-2-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/assets/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/ecfr_search_lymphedema.json)\n  - [ecfr_search_lymphedema_title42.json](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-2-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/assets/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/ecfr_search_lymphedema_title42.json)\n\n### 3.5. GPO GovInfo API\n- **Role:** External link target for legislative vehicles and public law summaries in the node inspection panel (Section 3.1 Item 5).\n- **Endpoint:** `GET https://api.govinfo.gov/packages/BILLS-117hr3630ih/summary?api_key=DEMO_KEY` (HTTP 200 OK, Content-Length: 69,576 bytes).\n- **Observed Schema:** `$.title`, `$.shortTitle[*].title` (`\"Lymphedema Treatment Act\"`), `$.congress` (`\"117\"`), `$.originChamber` (`\"HOUSE\"`), `$.references[*].{collectionCode: 'USCODE', contents: [{title: '42', sections: ['1395x']}]}`.\n- **Saved Ground-Truth Payload:**\n  - [govinfo_bills_117hr3630ih_summary.json](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-2-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/assets/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/govinfo_bills_117hr3630ih_summary.json)\n\n### 3.6. CMS Medicare Coverage Database (MCD)\n- **Role:** External link target for `CoveragePolicy` nodes (`CMS-MCD-A59508`, `CMS-MCD-A59588`) (Section 3.1 Item 5).\n- **Endpoint:** `GET https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=59508`\n- **Observed Response:** HTTP/2 503 (Akamai bot protection/CDN challenge). Direct external browser URLs link successfully for human users via browser context, but programmatic scrapers encounter Akamai WAF challenges.\n- **Saved Ground-Truth Payloads:**\n  - [cms_mcd_a59508_headers.txt](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-2-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/assets/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/cms_mcd_a59508_headers.txt)\n  - [cms_mcd_a59508_probe.html](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-2-20261013T025302-800-gxuw/assets/20261013T025302-800-gxuw/cms_mcd_a59508_probe.html)\n\n---\n\n## 4. Explicit Deficiency Register (INV-ABSENCE-01)\n\nIn strict accordance with `INV-ABSENCE-01`, specced requirements lacking providing components in the codebase or reachable external APIs are explicitly cataloged below without inventing synthetic components:\n\n| Deficiency ID | Specced Requirement | Functional Specification Clause | Current Codebase State | Exact Missing Capability |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **DEF-01** | Browser Graph Canvas Frontend Application | `functional_specification_004.md` Section 3.1 (`Browser Graph Canvas Requirements`) | Only design notes exist in `visualization.md`. The repository root `package.json` contains only `@ai-hero/sandcastle`. | Missing React frontend application, Vite/build config, graph rendering engine (Three.js / React Flow / Cytoscape), camera controls, and force-directed simulation layout. |\n| **DEF-02** | High-Cardinality Clustering \u0026 Paginated Fee Schedule Node Collapse | `functional_specification_004.md` Section 3.1 Item 4 (`Scalability \u0026 Node Clustering on High-Density Tiers`) | Backend produces 3,710 `:FeeScheduleEntry` nodes in `exports/lta_knowledge_graph.json` and 3,816 in Neo4j, but no UI abstraction exists. | Missing frontend clustering / expand-collapse filter to summarize 3,800+ fee schedule nodes by state or procedure code